763
00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:41.780
and they would tow it.

764
00:32:41.920 --> 00:32:45.420
So it looks like you're driving, but you're just being towed.

765
00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:47.700
Yeah, but you're really out on the road.

766
00:32:47.860 --> 00:32:48.040
Yeah.

767
00:32:48.940 --> 00:32:50.560
But that was not the case here.

768
00:32:50.760 --> 00:32:51.140
No.

769
00:32:51.320 --> 00:32:55.680
Dave said because of the amount of driving scenes and the earlier sunset times that come

770
00:32:55.680 --> 00:33:00.200
with daylight savings combined with a packed shooting schedule that included shooting

771
00:33:00.200 --> 00:33:04.900
numerous other scenes on the same day, Dave described that there were these plates that

772
00:33:04.900 --> 00:33:08.620
literally wrapped around the car, the front, sides, and back.

773
00:33:08.940 --> 00:33:11.360
And there were also screens in the front of the windshield.

774
00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:13.560
And here's what that looks like, you guys.

775
00:33:13.700 --> 00:33:15.040
Jenna and I have both done this.

776
00:33:15.160 --> 00:33:18.720
Like I did a driving scene for the television show, Better Things.

777
00:33:19.360 --> 00:33:26.700
And when they have plates around the car, it had like scenery on these big like screens.

778
00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:29.180
Was that your experience, Jenna?

779
00:33:29.460 --> 00:33:33.280
Well, he's calling them plates because that's the industry term, but I think it's more accurate

780
00:33:33.280 --> 00:33:37.260
to say they're like giant green screens that surround the car.

781
00:33:37.480 --> 00:33:45.620
And then they project the road onto it, the moving road onto these screens that surround the car.

782
00:33:45.620 --> 00:33:50.660
Yeah, there were like these huge squares on stands that surround the car.

783
00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:51.000
Yeah.

784
00:33:51.240 --> 00:33:56.000
And then they can put whatever they want on those big squares to show wherever you are.

785
00:33:56.180 --> 00:33:59.920
So my driving scene was in a city, they're in the country.

786
00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:04.720
Yeah, I did this for that television show I did in London called You, Me, and the Apocalypse.

787
00:34:06.060 --> 00:34:11.040
And it was crazy because like in this episode, there's going to be a moment where like Donal

788
00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:13.760
puts the window down, Ned puts the window down.

789
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:15.760
