790
00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:19.140
And so they have, it's like old timey fans.

791
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:24.600
And also like truly there's just some dudes in the back just like rocking the car.

792
00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:29.080
Yeah, I did find it kind of surreal because I'd only ever done driving scenes on the office

793
00:34:29.080 --> 00:34:30.480
where we were actually on the road.

794
00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:34.460
So the things I looked out the window were real trees I was passing and stuff like that.

795
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:38.300
And when I did my scene on Better Things, I'm in the back seat and we hit a bump.

796
00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:42.440
But it's kind of distracting because there's just like three men right outside.

797
00:34:42.840 --> 00:34:43.000
Yeah.

798
00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:44.820
Like kind of raising the car.

799
00:34:45.760 --> 00:34:45.840
Yeah.

800
00:34:45.940 --> 00:34:50.180
David said while there are pros and cons to using this technique, ultimately he felt like

801
00:34:50.180 --> 00:34:53.260
it looked pretty realistic and allowed them to have more shooting time.

802
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:55.480
And that took away a lot of pressure for everyone.

803
00:34:55.720 --> 00:34:57.780
And I think you see them having fun.

804
00:34:58.200 --> 00:34:59.920
I think it really paid off.

805
00:35:00.160 --> 00:35:01.260
They tricked me.

